            %p
          E.g.
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#Vogt71"} Vogt 1971, Prop. 1.2 (h)
          %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Homotopy+Theory#kificationComparisonIsWeakHomotopyEquivalence"} here
          at
          = succeed "." do
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} model structure on compactly generated topological spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean-generated+topological+spaces"} Euclidean-generated topological spaces
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Delta-generated+topological+spaces"}> Delta-generated topological spaces
                )
          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesCGHausdorffSpaces k-Spaces and CG Hausdorff spaces
          %p The idea of compactly generated Hausdorff spaces first appears in print in:
          %ul
            %li#Gale50
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gale"}> David Gale
              , Section 1 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Compact Sets of Functions and Function Rings
              %strong 1
              (1950) pp.303-308. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/proc/1950-001-03/S0002-9939-1950-0036503-X/S0002-9939-1950-0036503-X.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2032373"} doi:10.2307/2032373
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2032373"} jstor:2032373
          %p
            where it is attributed to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witold+Hurewicz"} Witold Hurewicz
            %sup#fnref:2
              %a{:href => "#fn:2", :rel => "footnote"} 2
          %p Early textbook accounts, assuming the Hausdorff condition:
          %ul
            %li#Kelley55
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Kelley"}> John Kelley
                , p. 230 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em General topology
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780387901251"} ISBN:978-0-387-90125-1
            %li#Dugundji66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dugundji"}> James Dugundji
                , Section XI.9 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.southalabama.edu/mathstat/personal_pages/carter/Dugundji.pdf"} pdf
            %li#GabrielZisman67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"}> Pierre Gabriel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Zisman"} Michel Zisman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calculus+of+fractions+and+homotopy+theory"} Calculus of fractions and homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/GZ.pdf"} pdf
          %p also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Susan+Niefield"}> Susan Niefield
                , Section 9 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cartesianness
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.proquest.com/docview/302920643"} proquest:302920643
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 7.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories and Structures
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                %strong 50
                Cambridge University Press (1994) (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525865"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525865
                )
          %p
            Influential emphasis of the usefulness of the notion as providing a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category of topological spaces
          %ul
            %li#Steenrod67
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Norman+Steenrod"}> Norman Steenrod
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A convenient category of topological spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.mmj/1028999711"} euclid:mmj/1028999711
          %p
            Early discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces"} geometric realization of simplicial topological spaces
          %ul
            %li#MacLane70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
              , Section 4 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Milgram bar construction as a tensor product of functors
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Steenrod Algebra and Its Applications: A Conference to Celebrate N.E. Steenrod’s Sixtieth Birthday
              = succeed "," do
                %em 168
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0058523"} doi:10.1007/BFb0058523
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/BFb0058523.pdf"} pdf
          %p and briefly in:
          %ul
            %li#May72
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              , Section 1 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The geometry of iterated loop spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/geom_iter.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0067491"} doi:10.1007/BFb0067491
          %p
            More history and early references, with emphasis on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            aspects:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horst+Herrlich"}> Horst Herrlich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Strecker"} George Strecker
              %em Categorical topology – Its origins as exemplified by the unfolding of the theory of topological reflections and coreflections before 1971
              (
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007%2F978-94-017-0468-7_15.pdf"}> pdf
              ), pages 255-341 in: C. E. Aull, R Lowen (eds.),
              %em Handbook of the History of General Topology. Vol. 1
              , Kluwer 1997 (
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-94-017-0468-7"}> doi:10.1007/978-94-017-0468-7
              )
          %p The terminology “kaonic spaces”, or rather the Russian version “каонные пространства” is used in
          %ul
            %li#Postnikov71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M+M+Postnikov"}> M M Postnikov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Введение в теорию Морса
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://libgen.is/book/index.php?md5=4BF450585846A0531FF485E34D062C0A"} web
            %li#Postnikov82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M+M+Postnikov"}> M M Postnikov
                , p. 34 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Лекции по алгебраической топологии. Основы теории гомотопий
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://libgen.is/book/index.php?md5=34A8C3C956EB80877F4E3CF5A297F514"} web
          %p
            Discussion of k-spaces in the generality of subcategory-generated spaces, including
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Delta-generated+topological+spaces"} Delta-generated topological spaces
          %ul
            %li#Vogt71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+M.+Vogt"}> Rainer M. Vogt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Convenient categories of topological spaces for homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01222616"} doi:10.1007/BF01222616
            %li#EscardoLawsonSimpson04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"}> Martín Escardó
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jimmie+Lawson"} Jimmie Lawson
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Simpson"} Alex Simpson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Comparing Cartesian closed categories of (core) compactly generated spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.topol.2004.02.011"} doi:10.1016/j.topol.2004.02.011
            %li#Gaucher07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philippe+Gaucher"}> Philippe Gaucher
                , Section 2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopical interpretation of globular complex by multipointed d-space
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0710.3553"} arXiv:0710.3553
          %p
            Proof that k-spaces form a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
          %ul
            %li#CagliariMatovaniVitale95
              F. Cagliari, S. Mantovani,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+Vitale"} Enrico Vitale
              = succeed "," do
                %em Regularity of the category of Kelley spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00872904"} doi:10.1007/BF00872904
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.dm.unibo.it/~cagliari/articoli/Regularkelley.pdf"} pdf
          %p Further accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+W.+Whitehead"}> George W. Whitehead
                , Section I.4 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elements of Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4612-6318-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-6318-0
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Day"}> Brian J. Day
                ,
                %em Relationship of Spanier’s Quasi-topological Spaces to k-Spaces
                , M. Sc. thesis University of Sydney 1968. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.mq.edu.au/~street/DayMasters.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Peter Booth, Philip R. Heath,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renzo+A.+Piccinini"} Renzo A. Piccinini
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibre preserving maps and functional spaces
            %li#Piccinini92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renzo+A.+Piccinini"}> Renzo A. Piccinini
                , Appendix B in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 171
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/north-holland-mathematics-studies/vol/171/suppl/C"} ISBN:978-0-444-89238-6
            %li#FelixHalperinThomas00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+F%C3%A9lix"}> Yves Félix
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Halperin"} Stephen Halperin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Claude+Thomas"} Jean-Claude Thomas
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rational Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4613-0105-9"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-0105-9
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in a context of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            %li#AGP02
              %p
                Marcelo Aguilar,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Gitler"} Samuel Gitler
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology from a homotopical viewpoint
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://tocs.ulb.tu-darmstadt.de/106999419.pdf"} toc pdf
            %li
              %p
                Samuel Smith,
                %em The homotopy theory of function spaces: a survey
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.0804"}> arXiv:1009.0804
                )
          %h3#ReferencesCGWeakHausdorffSpaces CG weak Hausdorff spaces
          %p The idea of generalizing compact generation to weakly Hausdorff spaces appears in:
          %ul
            %li#McCord69
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+C.+McCord"}> Michael C. McCord
              , Section 2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classifying Spaces and Infinite Symmetric Products
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1995173"} jstor:1995173
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/tran/1969-146-00/S0002-9947-1969-0251719-4/S0002-9947-1969-0251719-4.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            where it is attributed to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+C.+Moore"} John C. Moore
          %p Review in this generality of CG weakly Hausdorff spaces:
          %ul
            %li#Lewis78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaunce+Lewis"}> Gaunce Lewis
                ,
                %em Compactly generated spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/MISC/GaunceApp.pdf"}> pdf
                ), appendix A of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Stable Category and Generalized Thom Spectra
            %li#FritschPiccinini90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Fritsch"}> Rudolf Fritsch
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renzo+Piccinini"} Renzo Piccinini
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cellular structures in topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511983948"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511983948
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://epub.ub.uni-muenchen.de/4493/1/4493.pdf"} pdf
            %li#May99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                , Chapter 5 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+concise+course+in+algebraic+topology"} A concise course in algebraic topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/C/bo3777031.html"} ISBN: 9780226511832
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/CONCISE/ConciseRevised.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Strickland09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"}> Neil Strickland
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The category of CGWH spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://neil-strickland.staff.shef.ac.uk/courses/homotopy/cgwh.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StricklandCGHWSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Schwede12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                , Section A.2 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
                (2012)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Compactly Generated Spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://faculty.math.illinois.edu/~rezk/cg-spaces-better.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Rezk_CompactlyGeneratedSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Brief review in preparation of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} model structure on compactly generated topological spaces
          %ul
            %li#Hovey99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
              , Def. 2.4.21 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+Categories"} Model Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-63-s"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4361-1
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/surv/063"} doi:10.1090/surv/063
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/hovey-model-cats.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=Kfs4uuiTXN0C&printsec=frontcover"} Google books
          %p
            Review with focus on compactly generated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            and specifically
            = succeed "-theory:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+bundle"} equivariant bundle
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernardo+Uribe"}> Bernardo Uribe
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+L%C3%BCck"} Wolfgang Lück
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant principal bundles and their classifying spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.4862"} arXiv:1304.4862
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2140/agt.2014.14.1925"} doi:10.2140/agt.2014.14.1925
          %div
            %h3#ParameterizedTopology Exponential law for parameterized topological spaces
            %p
              On
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+law+for+spaces"} exponential objects
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+homs"}> internal homs
              ) in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
              of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"}> compactly generated
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              – see at
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+homotopy+theory"} parameterized homotopy theory
            %ul
              %li#Booth70
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+I.+Booth"}> Peter I. Booth
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Exponential Law of Maps I
                  %strong s3-20
                  1 (1970) 179-192
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/plms/s3-20.1.179"} doi:10.1112/plms/s3-20.1.179
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#Booth71
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+I.+Booth"}> Peter I. Booth
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The exponential law of maps. II
                  %strong 121
                  (1971) 311–319
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01109977"} doi:10.1007/BF01109977
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#BoothBrown78a
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+I.+Booth"}> Peter I. Booth
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Spaces of partial maps, fibred mapping spaces and the compact-open topology
                  %strong 8
                  2 (1978) 181-195
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0016-660X(78)90049-1"} doi:10.1016/0016-660X(78)90049-1
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#BoothBrown78b
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+I.+Booth"}> Peter I. Booth
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the application of fibred mapping spaces to exponential laws for bundles, ex-spaces and other categories of maps
                  %strong 8
                  2 (1978) 165-179
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0016-660X(78)90048-X"} doi:10.1016/0016-660X(78)90048-X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#Lewis85
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Gaunce+Lewis%2C+Jr."}> L. Gaunce Lewis, Jr.
                  , §1 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Open maps, colimits, and a convenient category of fibre spaces
                  %strong 19
                  1 (1985) 75-89
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0166-8641(85)90087-2"} doi.org/10.1016/0166-8641(85)90087-2
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              And with an eye towards
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+homotopy+theory"} parameterized homotopy theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"}> Ioan Mackenzie James
                  \: §II.9 in:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Fibrewise topology
                  = succeed "ISBN:9780521360906" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#MaySigurdsson06
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johann+Sigurdsson"} Johann Sigurdsson
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Parametrized+Homotopy+Theory"} Parametrized Homotopy Theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-132"} ISBN:978-0-8218-3922-5
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0411656"} arXiv:math/0411656
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/EXTHEORY/MaySig.pdf"} pdf
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  The reason for choosing the term “k-space” in
                  %a{:href => "#Gale50"} Gale 1950
                  seems to be lost in history. The “k” is not for “Kelley”, as
